# =============================================================================
# Hoptrail — .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# Lines are grouped by category with a comment header explaining the rationale
# for each group.
# =============================================================================

# --- Go build artifacts ---
# `go build` writes the binary to the working directory; the canonical binary
# name is 'hoptrail' (and 'hoptrail.exe' if a Windows build ever happens).
# 'main' catches accidental `go build` without -o. *.test catches test binaries
# left behind by `go test -c`. *.out catches profile and coverage outputs by
# default (more specific patterns below for clarity).
#
# Leading slash anchors these patterns to the repo root — without it, the
# bare 'hoptrail' rule would also match the cmd/hoptrail/ source directory
# at any depth, silently un-tracking the package's .go files (which is what
# happened from project init until step-25 caught it).
/hoptrail
/hoptrail.exe
/main
*.test
*.out

# --- Go cache / vendor ---
# Standard Go toolchain paths live outside the project tree, but a stray
# GOCACHE override or experimental tool could write them here. /vendor/ stays
# out unless vendored deps are adopted later; revisit if so.
/.gocache/
/vendor/

# --- Runtime data ---
# The SQLite database (and its WAL/SHM sidecars) is the user's probe history
# and should never appear in the source tree. The wildcard catches any *.db
# file, not just the canonical hoptrail.db, in case a developer creates a
# scratch DB during testing.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
hoptrail.pid

# --- Logs ---
# Where stdout/stderr gets captured during development:
#     hoptrail serve > logs/run.log 2>&1
# systemd-managed installs capture via journalctl and don't create logs/.
logs/

# --- Live config ---
# config.yaml is the user's live, customized configuration. The shipped
# template is config.yaml.example; the live config is generated from it on
# first install and edited per-user. Auto-merge backups (config.yaml.bak.*)
# stay out too.
config.yaml
config.yaml.bak.*

# --- Profiling / coverage output ---
# `go test -coverprofile=coverage.out` and pprof outputs.
coverage.out
coverage.html
profile.out
*.prof
*.pprof

# --- Frontend build output ---
# The Svelte+Vite UI source lives in web/src/ and web/public/; Vite
# writes its compiled output to internal/web/dist/ so the Go binary
# can embed it via embed.FS. A placeholder internal/web/dist/index.html
# is tracked so `go build` works on a fresh checkout before any
# `npm run build`; everything else under dist/ is build output and
# stays out of git (assets/ hashed bundles, copied public/ assets like
# favicon.svg).
internal/web/dist/*
!internal/web/dist/index.html
web/node_modules/

# --- Release artifacts ---
# `dist/` at the repo root holds packaged release tarballs + checksums
# destined for GitHub Releases; never committed.
/dist/
web/.svelte-kit/
web/.next/
web/.vite/

# --- Install backup snapshots ---
# An in-app updater (post-v0.1) would snapshot the live install before
# swapping in a new release. These are host-specific recovery state, not
# source. Defensive — the path doesn't exist yet but reserving the pattern.
.backups/

# --- Editor / IDE clutter ---
# Personal preferences, not project state.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- OS metadata ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Release artifacts ---
# Release tooling writes the release tarball (or zip) and .sha256 to the
# parent of the project tree, so they shouldn't normally land here. The
# patterns below are defensive — they keep accidental in-tree builds out of
# commits if the tooling is ever invoked from somewhere unexpected.
hoptrail-v*.tar.gz
hoptrail-v*.tar.gz.sha256
hoptrail-v*.zip
hoptrail-v*.zip.sha256

# --- Claude Code (maintainer-only, never public) ---
.claude/
HANDOFF*.md

# Internal design/decision docs — maintainer-only, never published
# (the public repo ships user/operator docs only).
/docs/design/

# Maintainer-only: live vulnerability findings — NEVER commit to the public repo
SECURITY-AUDIT*.md
